1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,461
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:08,008
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,226
[Martina] <i>We need to find someone</i>

7
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:21,646
<i>who can pretend</i>
<i>to be Ibyang's real mother.</i>

8
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,857
[Ame] <i>Atoy! She's Ibyang's mother!</i>

9
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,233
[Olga] <i>Where is she?</i>

10
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:28,361
[Atoy] <i>How can I be sure</i>
<i>you're really Ibyang's mother?</i>

11
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:29,863
[Olga] <i>Martin is my ex.</i>

12
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:31,614
<i>He's Ibyang's real father.</i>

13
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,992
Are you really my mama?

14
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:36,244
[Olga] <i>We'll be together now.</i>

15
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:39,873
<i>And if you'll agree, we'll go home.</i>

16
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,332
<i>I can't relax.</i>

17
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:42,667
Oh. Why?

18
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:45,837
[Olga] <i>Because of Atoy.</i>
<i>He's so suspicious of me!</i>

19
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:49,591
[Atoy] You will request
a maternity match test.

20
00:00:49,674 --> 00:00:50,592
And it's rush.

21
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:51,801
Okay.

22
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:53,052
This role is crucial.

23
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:55,472
[Olga] <i>We'll go inside</i>
<i>that tailoring shop.</i>

24
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:58,892
<i>Then we'll pretend to be a wealthy couple.</i>

25
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:01,311
<i>You need to distract him. Okay? Clear?</i>

26
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:02,228
[henchman] <i>Clear, ma'am.</i>

27
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:04,606
What about Brother Atoy?

28
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:06,733
[T-Bak] <i>Then he'll go solo in life!</i>

29
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:09,819
Positive, Emerson.
She really is the mother.

30
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:12,447
Hello, Atoy! I'll fetch Ibyang.

31
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:14,282
Where's Olga? Why--

32
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:16,785
Olga is at home, cleaning.

33
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:18,870
Preparing for Ibyang's arrival.

34
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:20,622
Will Ibyang take long?

35
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:22,665
- I'll just call her.
- Ah, okay.

36
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:25,210
PREVIOUSLY

37
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:26,878
♪ <i>Fix this </i> ♪

38
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:30,423
Oh, I'll pass by Brother Atoy's.

39
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,634
Sis Ame said Ibyang is leaving today.

40
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:35,428
- I'll come too.
- Okay.

41
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:37,222
[chuckles] All right.

42
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:38,598
Ibyang!

43
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:40,600
- Ibyang!
- Baby girl!

44
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:42,185
- [in English] How are you?
- Hey!

45
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:44,604
You're leaving today, baby girl?

46
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:46,397
Yes.

47
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:50,110
I want to say goodbye to all of you.

48
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:55,115
Ibyang, always take care. Be a good girl.

49
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:59,577
[in English] Ibyang, when you come
visit us next time, free pares on me.

50
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:01,746
- Hmm? [chuckles softly]
- [Siony] Hey, quiet!

51
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,373
You're stealing the moment!

52
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:07,710
Child, we'll miss you.

53
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:10,672
I'll miss you too.

54
00:02:10,755 --> 00:02:12,465
So much!

55
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:15,218
- Like ten million misses!
- Oh, that's a lot.

56
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:16,928
- That's too much.
- [chuckles]

57
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:18,388
[Nestor] That's a lot, huh.

58
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,224
[Emerson] Ibyang! Wait, wait.

59
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:26,563
Ibyang, don't be too naughty
at your mom. Okay?

60
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:30,483
Take care of yourself, Ibyang.

61
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:33,236
Study well. Don't be like me.

62
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:37,365
Yes, Sister Karla, Brother Emerson.

63
00:02:39,117 --> 00:02:40,034
[Cita] Ibyang!

64
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:43,329
Oh? Miss Cita.

65
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:45,123
[melancholic music playing]

66
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:46,499
Where's Sister Ame?

67
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:50,253
Don't worry, she's with us
here in Tabang Lupa.

68
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:52,255
We won't abandon her.

69
00:02:52,922 --> 00:02:54,591
And Tatoy too.

70
00:02:57,635 --> 00:02:59,554
San Antonio de Padua!

71
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:04,100
Thank you that Ibyang
has found her mother.

72
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:10,231
And Lord, please guide
this good child every day.

73
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:12,901
Bless you, Ibyang.

74
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:15,194
[all] Amen!

75
00:03:16,487 --> 00:03:17,947
Thank you.

76
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:21,117
- Take care, okay?
- I will.

77
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:35,423
- Take care, okay.
- Yes.

78
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:38,843
Yes. Bye-bye. Take care.

79
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:42,972
[inaudible]

80
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:59,197
[suave theme music playing]

81
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:28,601
Here, I'm giving you a cellphone.

82
00:04:29,852 --> 00:04:31,562
It's yours now.

83
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:34,565
I want you to use it.

84
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:37,694
I want you to use it responsibly, okay?

85
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:39,988
No social media.
Social media is forbidden.

86
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:43,449
I'll put it in your bag. Okay?

87
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:45,660
I want you to call me.

88
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:47,954
You've memorized my number, right?

89
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:51,165
I memorized your number,
but I also saved mine there just in case.

90
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:53,084
- [in English] Okay?
- [in English] Okay.

91
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,884
[gentle music playing]

92
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:03,094
[in English] Take care.

93
00:05:03,177 --> 00:05:05,305
Tell Olga to call me

94
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:07,098
- [Charmi] Ah, okay.
- if you need anything.

95
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:08,433
[Charmi] I'll tell her.

96
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:10,059
Ibyang, get inside!

97
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,770
[car door clicks shut]

98
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:22,447
[sentimental music playing]

99
00:06:56,666 --> 00:07:00,211
[Ibyang] Someday,
you'll need me in your missions.

100
00:07:00,294 --> 00:07:02,380
I don't need anyone to help me.

101
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:05,341
You'll swallow your words,

102
00:07:06,175 --> 00:07:08,678
and you'll choke! [coughs]

103
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:11,264
[Ibyang] <i>No one will bring you water,</i>

104
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:13,724
<i>except me!</i>

105
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:15,893
<i>Tatoy,</i>

106
00:07:16,477 --> 00:07:18,271
<i>thank you for your love.</i>

107
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:23,192
<i>Every day, I feel it,</i>

108
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:25,194
<i>even if you're not my real father.</i>

109
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:29,949
<i>In my heart, you're the true hero.</i>

110
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:33,578
<i>Thank you for everything, Tatoy.</i>

111
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:36,581
I love you, Tatoy!

112
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:39,792
I love you too, Ibyang.

113
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:41,961
My Tatoy.

114
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:47,467
[music fades]

115
00:07:48,551 --> 00:07:50,344
[engines whirring]

116
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:54,432
Please stop, please!
Wait. Please stop, please!

117
00:07:57,602 --> 00:08:01,689
[epic music playing]

118
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,067
<i>Tatoy!</i>

119
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:38,059
What are you still doing here?

120
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,143
[sobbing]

121
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:43,314
Your mother is waiting for you.
You need to go to her.

122
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:46,609
[sobbing]

123
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:47,944
Tatoy,

124
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,989
I just want to hug you again.

125
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:58,162
Don't neglect yourself, okay?

126
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,622
[sobbing]

127
00:08:59,705 --> 00:09:02,333
Eat well.

128
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:07,463
Don't be grumpy with your customers, okay?

129
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:09,507
- [chuckles]
- [sobbing]

130
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:14,011
Always be happy.

131
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,974
So I won't worry about you.

132
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:19,225
[sobs]

133
00:09:19,308 --> 00:09:22,311
You're not allowed to die
on your missions.

134
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:27,233
Yes, yes.

135
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:29,485
[sobbing]

136
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:32,029
Thank you, Tatoy.

137
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:33,573
[sobbing]

138
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:39,412
If not for you,
I wouldn't have had a family.

139
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:42,498
- [sobbing]
- [sentimental music playing]

140
00:09:43,457 --> 00:09:49,630
No one can replace you because I love you.

141
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:55,386
Thank you too.

142
00:09:56,429 --> 00:10:00,182
Because you know, because of you…

143
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:03,227
When you came into my life…

144
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:07,315
I got to know myself better.

145
00:10:08,566 --> 00:10:10,192
[Ibyang sobbing]

146
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,154
That's why I love you so much, Ibyang.

147
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:16,365
I'll miss you.

148
00:10:17,074 --> 00:10:18,743
[sobbing]

149
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:22,580
You'll always… always be stitched…

150
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:24,832
right here in my heart.

151
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:28,711
- Okay?
- [sobbing]

152
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:31,589
Take care, okay? Take care.

153
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:35,551
Okay? Be good. Okay?

154
00:10:36,218 --> 00:10:39,263
- [Atoy] Go now.
- [sobbing]

155
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:04,705
Go. Just keep me updated.

156
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:09,960
[in English] You look disappointed.

157
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:13,923
But I have something that's gonna
put a smile on your face.

158
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:15,424
[sinister music playing]

159
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,967
Olga has Ibyang now.

160
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:19,136
Good thing Atoy agreed.

161
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:23,015
Yes. But now that we have the kid,
what's your plan?

162
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:25,935
[suspicious music playing]

163
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:30,147
As long as we have Ibyang,
Atoy can't do anything against us.

164
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:31,899
The child is our trump card.

165
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:34,735
Hon, I get that.

166
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:36,278
But what?

167
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:38,656
The child will stay with Olga forever?

168
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:40,199
We'll raise Audrey's daughter?

169
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:41,909
Of course not.

170
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:45,329
So, what then?

171
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:49,166
Eventually, the child
has to be disposed of.

172
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,960
What do you mean, disposed of?

173
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:56,632
Ah, maybe included in a shipment or…

174
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:59,593
Get rid of her, so there's no trace.

175
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:00,719
[Martina scoffs]

176
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:03,180
[in English] Hon, she's just a child.

177
00:12:03,764 --> 00:12:05,599
I don't want to be a part of that.

178
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:09,186
Who said you'd be the one to do it?

179
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:15,401
[in English] I'll do it.

180
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:19,321
[tense music playing]

181
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:32,751
Come in.

182
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,297
[sighs]

183
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:40,801
[Olga] Are you hungry?

184
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:44,805
There's still food in the fridge.

185
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:46,474
Go ahead and get some.

186
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:02,990
Ma, why did you put this in the fridge?

187
00:13:03,782 --> 00:13:04,992
It's spoiled already.

188
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:08,579
[pensive music playing]

189
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:12,333
[in English] Sorry.

190
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:17,338
[Olga] Better fix your things upstairs.

191
00:13:17,421 --> 00:13:19,673
Hmm? I'll just go to the supermarket.

192
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:22,593
The mall nearby, the one you saw earlier.

193
00:13:22,676 --> 00:13:24,553
Your room is upstairs.

194
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:26,680
- Okay.
- Wait.

195
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:29,475
You're leaving me here?

196
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:31,977
I'll be quick.

197
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:33,312
It won't take long, okay?

198
00:13:40,819 --> 00:13:41,654
Hey!

199
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:45,908
Aren't you going to wait for your child?

200
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:48,827
She'll be fine.

201
00:13:59,421 --> 00:14:02,091
[sneaky music playing]

202
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:14,436
Sister Olga, my project, okay?
It's almost due.

203
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:18,566
Relax. It's almost done. Just wait.

204
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:21,235
And don't forget the payment.

205
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:22,194
[in English] Okay?

206
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:23,404
[in English] Thank you!

207
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:24,446
[Olga chuckles softly]

208
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,240
She's hustling.

209
00:14:26,323 --> 00:14:27,825
She's hustling, oh!

210
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:31,287
Oh, small-time hustle
like doing student projects,

211
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:32,496
and you already have money.

212
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:35,541
- Oh! Wait. Speaking of money.
- Mmm?

213
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:39,920
- Here she comes! Fifty K!
- Huh? Hmm!

214
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:42,423
She got money right away,
just pretending to be Faye.

215
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:43,883
[giggles]

216
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:44,884
Told you so.

217
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:48,888
Hey, have you thought about it?
Where could Ibyang's real mother be?

218
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:51,891
Now you're asking,
when you already have the money.

219
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:53,893
- Forget it.
- No.

220
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:58,022
Because what if Ibyang's real mother
is really looking for her?

221
00:14:58,105 --> 00:15:00,149
So what? You feel guilty?

222
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:01,483
Then let's just return the money.

223
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:04,445
- Give it to me.
- No. No, no, hey, hey. I'm just curious.

224
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:06,155
Because the child is so kind.

225
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:08,616
She's easy to love, right?

226
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:11,911
Oh, now you must act like a full-time mom.

227
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:14,830
What about your dream
of being rich and famous?

228
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:15,831
Hmm.

229
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,667
Just wait. It'll come.

230
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:20,669
For now, this hustle will do, right?

231
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:21,921
This isn't forever.

232
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:24,256
What's important is I'm getting paid.

233
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,592
So, even if I have to act
like a single mom all day,

234
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:28,052
I can handle it.

235
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:29,261
Go!

236
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:30,179
Mmm.

237
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:31,680
- What?
- Oh!

238
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:32,848
You know what?

239
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:37,603
Your child should have a father too,
so it's a complete family!

240
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:39,939
Oh! Atoy could be a candidate.

241
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:41,774
- Eh!
- He's handsome,

242
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,525
Ibyang knows him, and--

243
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:47,112
- Oh. You have history! Ohh.
- [in English] Past is past.

244
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:48,656
And besides, I don't want
to share the money.

245
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:50,491
This racket is mine alone.

246
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:52,326
That's right.

247
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:53,577
You're right.

248
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:56,121
Okay, fine. I have to go.
I'll go now, okay?

249
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,791
Hey, wait. Aren't you coming
with me to the grocery store?

250
00:15:58,874 --> 00:15:59,792
Oh.

251
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:02,878
No, you can handle it!

252
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:06,090
I'll just check out what's in my cart.
I already have money.

253
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,132
So arrogant!

254
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:09,677
- [giggles] Bye-bye!
- Okay then.

255
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:24,233
[somber music playing]

256
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:26,193
Miss!

257
00:16:27,277 --> 00:16:29,530
- Psst. You're too noisy!
- [chuckles]

258
00:16:29,613 --> 00:16:32,199
They might hear you. Is Atoy there?

259
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:33,951
Yes.

260
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:37,538
He's there. We're
just drowning his sadness.

261
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:38,747
He invited us.

262
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,290
[Emerson chuckles softly]

263
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:41,583
Don't leave him, okay?

264
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:42,835
Stay with him.

265
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:44,128
No.

266
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:45,379
Of course.

267
00:16:45,462 --> 00:16:49,091
Well… Well, as long
as he pays for the drinks.

268
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:51,427
- Me, I'll just be the server.
- Hmm?

269
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,178
No, just kidding.

270
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:55,389
Come on, miss. You're too serious.

271
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:59,143
I'm just joking,
because that's what I do to him also.

272
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:00,477
I just joke with him,

273
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:05,274
so he'll smile a little,
despite what he's going through.

274
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:07,192
Will you talk to him?

275
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:11,321
Even if I want to,
I don't think he'll talk to me.

276
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,614
Hmm.

277
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:15,659
[somber music playing]

278
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:18,078
Oh.

279
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:23,667
Ah, fried dumpling,
with vinegar and sweet sauce.

280
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:26,128
You should buy that.

281
00:17:26,211 --> 00:17:28,297
It's their favorite, his and Ibyang's.

282
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:32,634
- Take charge, okay?
- Yes, sir. Okay.

283
00:17:32,718 --> 00:17:33,802
[Emerson chuckles softly]

284
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:43,479
[Olga] Ibyang!

285
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:47,858
Sorry. I got home late!
So many people at the groce--

286
00:17:47,941 --> 00:17:50,694
[pensive music playing]

287
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:54,656
Is this my house?

288
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,873
Ma, let's eat.

289
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:04,458
I cooked.

290
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,475
[pensive music playing]

291
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:23,811
[Olga] You're unbelievable!

292
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:33,028
You opened the imported corned beef?!

293
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,615
[sighs]

294
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:38,867
[Olga] You child.
That's Sam-Sam's favorite.

295
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:41,578
Who's Sam?

296
00:18:42,412 --> 00:18:43,789
Your boyfriend?

297
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,666
My father?

298
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:47,501
No!

299
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:53,048
Anyway, you shouldn't touch
my things here!

300
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:06,019
Where's my basket?

301
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:07,980
[suspicious music playing]

302
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:13,318
Um…

303
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,197
I threw it away.

304
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:20,868
I thought it was trash.

305
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:22,911
What?!

306
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:24,663
[tense music playing]

307
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:28,792
Oh, no! Why did you do that?!

308
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:31,420
[music intensifies]

309
00:19:31,503 --> 00:19:35,716
From now on, you won't touch
any of my things here!

310
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,801
[in English] Okay?! Huh?!

311
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:41,513
I don't-- I don't even know
where my things are anymore!

312
00:19:42,097 --> 00:19:44,224
You shouldn't have done that!

313
00:19:44,308 --> 00:19:45,142
[pensive music playing]

314
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,603
You should've just left it messy!

315
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:50,022
Okay? You shouldn't have touched it!

316
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,649
You are unbelievable!

317
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:56,069
[dramatic music playing]

318
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:04,578
[gasping]

319
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:12,294
Oh my!

320
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:17,799
[Emerson exhales]

321
00:20:19,426 --> 00:20:21,136
See?

322
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,554
[utensils clatter]

323
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:26,183
Oh, here… Here.

324
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:30,729
This is perfect. Oh, 'Toy, fish. Right?

325
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:38,070
What does the fish say,
and why does it go to the priest?

326
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:39,071
Go on.

327
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:40,155
[quirky music playing]

328
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:44,284
To… con-fish.

329
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:46,536
[chuckles]

330
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:49,373
The priest said, "Fish be with you."

331
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:50,958
[chuckles]

332
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:53,210
It's still hot. Oh, milkfish!

333
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:55,212
Right?

334
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:58,840
What does the milkfish say
when it's about to die?

335
00:20:59,549 --> 00:21:00,425
[Atoy] What?

336
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:02,135
[groans]

337
00:21:02,219 --> 00:21:03,470
[in English] I'm <i>daing</i>.

338
00:21:03,553 --> 00:21:06,807
[babbling, laughs]

339
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:09,101
Whoo! There you go.

340
00:21:09,685 --> 00:21:10,811
Sorry, bro.

341
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:15,232
I know you're just trying
to make me laugh, but…

342
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:17,401
[sighs]

343
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:19,987
It's really hard
to fend off loneliness, isn't it?

344
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:22,072
[melancholic music playing]

345
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:23,782
Think about it. Just recently…

346
00:21:26,243 --> 00:21:28,078
Ibyang was given to me.

347
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:31,999
Then, my family.

348
00:21:34,209 --> 00:21:36,128
And now they're all gone.

349
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:39,589
They came quickly, but…

350
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:42,467
were taken from me just as fast.

351
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:46,722
[scoffs]

352
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:48,390
I'm fine.

353
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,476
[exhales, then clears throat]

354
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:52,894
I'm used to it.

355
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,355
I can handle being alone.

356
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:58,650
But why is it like that?

357
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:04,031
They made me feel happiness.

358
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:06,908
Then… [scoffs]

359
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:11,580
Just like that,
they're suddenly taken away.

360
00:22:20,797 --> 00:22:21,923
You know, 'Toy…

361
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:27,637
you're not the only one
who feels that way.

362
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:28,680
[chuckles softly]

363
00:22:31,475 --> 00:22:33,643
I feel that too, with Tonet.

364
00:22:35,604 --> 00:22:37,314
Because, you know…

365
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:38,482
[giggles]

366
00:22:38,565 --> 00:22:40,525
[sentimental music playing]

367
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:41,818
She was gone for so long.

368
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:44,196
Gone from my life, and…

369
00:22:46,364 --> 00:22:48,366
when she came back, it didn't last.

370
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:50,202
It was so fast.

371
00:22:52,412 --> 00:22:53,914
She was taken so quickly.

372
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:57,501
But you know…

373
00:23:00,253 --> 00:23:01,505
every day…

374
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:06,802
Even if it's hard to accept…

375
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:10,722
I fight it off, but… I miss her, bro.

376
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,224
[Emerson chuckles softly]

377
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:17,062
I miss her, bro.

378
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,231
I miss my sister.

379
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:22,984
[melodramatic music playing]

380
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:25,779
[chuckles]

381
00:23:26,613 --> 00:23:27,447
'Toy…

382
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:28,365
[bottles clink]

383
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:29,574
Bro, come on--

384
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:30,867
I'm fine.

385
00:23:32,661 --> 00:23:35,247
Ah, you're making me sad. I'm fine.

386
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:38,291
It's hard, but I accept it. That's that.

387
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:42,170
[sniffs, then sighs]

388
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:43,338
You, what's your plan?

389
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:47,259
Life goes on.

390
00:23:49,594 --> 00:23:50,470
[chuckles softly]

391
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:52,514
Life goes on.

392
00:23:53,014 --> 00:23:54,641
To moving forward in life.

393
00:23:57,394 --> 00:23:58,311
[thuds]

394
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:06,945
[sniffs, then sighs]

395
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:10,907
[Emerson] Hey. [clears throat]

396
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:13,160
[Emerson] Boss.

397
00:24:13,243 --> 00:24:15,036
Ah, well.

398
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:15,996
[pensive music playing]

399
00:24:16,079 --> 00:24:19,166
If you're having a suit tailored,
just come back later.

400
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:21,835
The Master Cutter's chops have dropped.

401
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:23,170
He's a bit down in life.

402
00:24:24,004 --> 00:24:25,088
Just come back, sir.

403
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:26,214
[suspicious music playing]

404
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:29,217
[in English] Captain Padua, this is
Lieutenant Gonzales reporting.

405
00:24:30,218 --> 00:24:32,262
[in English] I was ordered
by Colonel Mercado to meet you

406
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:33,680
and deliver his directives.

407
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:37,058
[suspicious music playing]

408
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:39,269
Ah… [titters]

409
00:24:39,352 --> 00:24:40,979
[Emerson] Cool.

410
00:24:41,062 --> 00:24:43,607
You're connected
with Boss Mercado and Atoy?

411
00:24:44,983 --> 00:24:46,067
[Emerson] Impressive!

412
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:48,069
[electronic blipping]

413
00:24:53,158 --> 00:24:55,785
Emerson here, sir. Emerson Mendoza.

414
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:02,292
Sir, I need him cleared out.
[in English] Mission protocol.

415
00:25:03,043 --> 00:25:05,086
Colonel Mercado will call soon.

416
00:25:06,796 --> 00:25:09,049
No, no. Boss. [chuckles]

417
00:25:09,132 --> 00:25:11,176
It's fine. No, it's fine--

418
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:14,679
He's with me. I'm part of Atoy's missions.

419
00:25:14,763 --> 00:25:16,514
I'm his coworker.

420
00:25:16,598 --> 00:25:18,350
And don't worry, sir.

421
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:20,310
I'm not a gossip. Ah, sir.

422
00:25:20,393 --> 00:25:23,021
[in English] No, no, no. He's good.
He's good, he's good.

423
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:36,826
[in English] What is your name?

424
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:39,704
[in English] We are the Sokolov brothers.

425
00:25:39,788 --> 00:25:42,040
[suspicious music playing]

426
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,627
[in Russian] Damn it!

427
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:48,129
[in English] Even the window cleaner.

428
00:25:50,507 --> 00:25:51,967
[laptop blips]

429
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:54,970
[security guard, in English] We used AI
to see what he might look like.

430
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:56,137
[in English] The photos matched.

431
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:03,979
[in English] I want you
to find out everything about this man.

432
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:08,066
[in English] We tried, sir.

433
00:26:08,149 --> 00:26:10,986
[in English] But unfortunately, no trace.

434
00:26:17,951 --> 00:26:21,579
[in English] Then, we will find him.

435
00:26:22,706 --> 00:26:26,251
[in English] I'm sure
he is looking for the decoder.

436
00:26:29,754 --> 00:26:31,881
[electronic blipping]

437
00:26:39,931 --> 00:26:43,059
The Master Cutter isn't here right now.

438
00:26:43,143 --> 00:26:45,103
[Cita] He already has another assignment.

439
00:26:45,186 --> 00:26:47,397
It's over! We have no hope!

440
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:52,610
Calm down. We'll try
to contact another tracker.

441
00:26:52,694 --> 00:26:54,571
Huh? Who?

442
00:26:54,654 --> 00:26:56,781
The… The child.

443
00:26:56,865 --> 00:26:58,908
[Emerson] <i>The child, child of a thread.</i>

444
00:26:58,992 --> 00:26:59,826
Hello, Atoy.

445
00:26:59,909 --> 00:27:03,288
We found the suspect
in the five-million robbery.

446
00:27:03,371 --> 00:27:05,749
I thought of something
we could profit from.

447
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:07,167
[Olga] <i>That's a big amount of money.</i>

448
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:08,418
How much are you selling this for?

449
00:27:08,501 --> 00:27:09,836
[in English] It's already sold.

450
00:27:09,919 --> 00:27:13,631
- [in English] Scam! Scammer!
- Mama?

451
00:27:13,715 --> 00:27:16,051
[Mercado, in English] <i>The laptop is locked</i>
<i>and requires a code.</i>

452
00:27:16,134 --> 00:27:17,677
<i>Aside from the ambassador,</i>

453
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:22,724
<i>the only person who knows the code</i>
<i>is the head of IT at the embassy.</i>

454
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:25,477
<i>Your mission, get him.</i>

455
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:27,979
UP NEXT

456
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:34,027
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
